# Generated exe crash gate (N7 / FEAT-4G startup)

## Scope split

| Target | Protection |
|--------|------------|
| `dev\tcc.exe` | C1 VEH in `tcc.c` — compiler AV -> diagnostic exit 1 |
| Generated `*.exe` | **No VEH** — bad `.init_array` startup -> WER before main |

Compile success / link success **does not** mean startup is safe.

## Binary roles

- `dev\tcc.exe` — last-known-good only (never overwrite with 01B WIP).
- `dev\tcc_wip.exe` — 01B experiments only.
- Never treat `%TEMP%\tcc_n7_*` exe as authority; do not re-run crashed exe.

## Mandatory workflow

1. **compile-only** — `n7_cross_01b_compile_only.bat` with `TCC_EXE=..\..\..\tcc_wip.exe` and `N7_01B_COMPILE_GATE=POST`. **No run.**
2. **Static check** (optional) — `dumpbin /SECTION:.text /DISASM` on fresh exe; init thunk must store to **`.bss` / writable `.data`**, not `.rdata`.
3. **Single run** — one fresh compile, one run, only after (1) is green and user or plan allows.
4. **Full run gate** — `n7_cross_01b_measure.bat` only after single-run passes.

## Forbidden

- Running `n7_cross_01b_measure.bat` or any `:run` bat while 01B WIP is unverified.
- Using compile-only PASS as permission to batch-run exe.
- Re-running a WER-crash exe for "one more try".

## Known runtime failure pattern (01B)

Global `const T g = expr()` copy-init: if storage lands in **rodata**, startup copy-init **AV**. Fix: allocate writable storage at decl time (`type.t &= ~VT_CONSTANT` before `decl_initializer_alloc` for dynamic copy-init).
